= The Red Army of Bavaria

Munich has a few thousand armed workers, some regiments of the old garrison that have elected their officers, and a great many speeches. Egelhofer wants every worker armed. The former officers who have come over want ranks, drill and obedience. The councils want the bourgeoisie disarmed first.

- @arm_all: Arm every worker who will take a rifle.
- @discipline: Give the army officers and discipline.
- @disarm: Disarm the bourgeoisie and take hostages.

@arm_all
subtitle: The Left's answer, and Egelhofer's. Many rifles, little training.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 8; red_guards_strength += 4; red_guards_arms += 4; militancy += 4; offensive_satisfaction += 5; lean_offensive += 2

Rifles from the barracks are handed out at factory gates against a membership card or a council stamp. By the end of the week the Red Army has twenty thousand names on its lists.

@discipline
subtitle: The Spartacist and the Right's choice: a smaller army that can actually fight.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 6; red_guards_strength += 2; red_guards_arms += 6; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3; unionist_satisfaction += 3; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 4; lean_luxemburgist += 1; lean_unionist += 1

Elected officers get the right to give orders in battle. The anarchists protest. The battalions that train behave like soldiers when the shooting starts.

@disarm
subtitle: The Left Radicals' class war. It strengthens us now, and gives the Whites their atrocity stories.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 6; red_guards_arms += 5; repression += 4; bav_hostages = 1; ultraleft_satisfaction += 5; offensive_satisfaction += 3; lean_ultraleft += 2

Red Guards search the villas of Bogenhausen for weapons and take the owners away for questioning. Some of them are not released.
